Below is a progressive set of exploratory → final queries (all limited to 20 rows) that surface repositories which depend on popular “feature-toggle” libraries.  
Every query is wrapped in a ```sql``` block and preceded by a short description.

```sql
-- 1. Quick peek at repository-level dependencies (any subject, first 20 rows)
SELECT *
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies`
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Find distinct dependency project names that contain “unleash”
SELECT DISTINCT dependency_project_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies`
WHERE  LOWER(dependency_project_name) LIKE '%unleash%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Same idea for “launchdarkly”
SELECT DISTINCT dependency_project_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies`
WHERE  LOWER(dependency_project_name) LIKE '%launchdarkly%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect how the “launchdarkly” projects look inside the Projects table
SELECT id,
       platform,
       name         AS project_name,
       language,
       licenses
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.projects`
WHERE  LOWER(name) LIKE '%launchdarkly%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Join repository_dependencies → repositories for repos that depend on “launchdarkly”
SELECT rd.repository_name_with_owner,
       r.host_type,
       r.size,
       r.language,
       rd.dependency_project_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` AS rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           AS r
       ON rd.repository_id = r.id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%launchdarkly%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same style join, but for any dependency whose name includes “unleash”
SELECT rd.repository_name_with_owner,
       r.host_type,
       r.size,
       r.language,
       rd.dependency_project_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` AS rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           AS r
       ON rd.repository_id = r.id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%unleash%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. How many repositories depend on each feature-toggle library (top 20 counts)
SELECT rd.dependency_project_name,
       COUNT(DISTINCT rd.repository_id) AS repos_using_library
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` AS rd
WHERE  REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name),
        r'(unleash|launchdarkly|togglz|ff4j|featuretoggle|featureswitcher|
          toggle|flipper|flipit|fflip|bandiera)')
GROUP  BY rd.dependency_project_name
ORDER  BY repos_using_library DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Bring in the Projects table to see the primary language of the library itself
SELECT rd.dependency_project_name      AS artifact_name,
       p.platform                      AS artifact_platform,
       p.language                      AS library_primary_language,
       COUNT(DISTINCT rd.repository_id) AS repos_using_library
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` AS rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.projects`               AS p
       ON rd.dependency_project_id = p.id
WHERE  REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name),
        r'(unleash|launchdarkly|togglz|ff4j|featuretoggle|featureswitcher|
          toggle|flipper|flipit|fflip|bandiera)')
GROUP  BY artifact_name, artifact_platform, library_primary_language
ORDER  BY repos_using_library DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9. FINAL: full repository details for repos that depend on any selected feature-toggle library
SELECT DISTINCT
       r.name_with_owner                       AS full_name_with_owner,
       r.host_type,
       r.size * 1024                           AS size_in_bytes,
       r.language                              AS primary_language,
       r.fork_source_name_with_owner           AS fork_source_name,
       r.updated_timestamp                     AS repo_last_update,
       rd.dependency_project_name              AS artifact_name,
       p.name                                  AS library_project_name,
       p.language                              AS library_primary_language
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` AS rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           AS r
       ON rd.repository_id = r.id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.projects`               AS p
       ON rd.dependency_project_id = p.id
WHERE  REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name),
        r'(unleash|launchdarkly|togglz|ff4j|featuretoggle|featureswitcher|
          toggle|flipper|flipit|fflip|bandiera)')
LIMIT  20;
```

Each successive query builds knowledge about where and how feature-toggle libraries appear, culminating in the final query that returns the repository-level information requested (one row per repository-library pairing, capped at 20 for inspection).
